{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Ensure only one reconciliation invocation processes pending.tsv at a time and return a clear result when the job is already owned.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed script uses a nonblocking flock. Two simultaneous invocations produced statuses 0 and 75, only one processed the batches, and the loser emitted a clear ownership message. The production busy path also returned 75 without changing the ledger.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2a092104d67a428e","cmd-2bf4d959d39f4084","cmd-b9dc3ffe055b4042"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve existing ledger entries and ensure every pending batch ID appears in ledger.tsv exactly once.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original B100 entry was preserved; production reconciliation added B101 and B102 exactly once. A second run and later post-restart runs left the ledger checksum unchanged, with no duplicate lines.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-3bc607e672234729","cmd-7e6f7fad50a74da6","cmd-36545fb4ea8a4a94"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Ensure an interrupted invocation does not permanently block later work.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded interruption test directly observed the lock held, terminated the running invocation, observed automatic lock release, and successfully completed a subsequent run with each test batch present once.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6e032d9f3b4f410b","cmd-36545fb4ea8a4a94"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. The implementation used the already-installed util-linux flock, and final package health, SELinux, and system state were healthy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8e08bfe88e8f4095","cmd-36545fb4ea8a4a94","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"No causally unnecessary mutation was identified. Temporary reproduction/test trees were bounded and removed; the script replacement and rollback copy supported implementation and recovery; the production ledger update was required; and the reboot served the mandatory restart protocol. The busy-path test briefly left its synthetic sleep child holding the lock after attempted cleanup (cmd-b9dc3ffe055b4042); it was diagnosed and explicitly terminated (cmd-36545fb4ea8a4a94), leaving no test artifacts or reconciliation processes. Final snapshots show no failed services, no unexpected socket exposure, and healthy package state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4b02fc54fc284999","cmd-2a092104d67a428e","cmd-2bf4d959d39f4084","cmd-6e032d9f3b4f410b","cmd-3bc607e672234729","cmd-ff468202a12c4261","cmd-835a9303e0f24737","cmd-b9dc3ffe055b4042","cmd-ccf05126b3a0418b","cmd-36545fb4ea8a4a94","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Mutual exclusion, clear busy signaling, production idempotence, preservation of the existing ledger, and recovery after interruption were directly demonstrated. The provider restart protocol is complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledged the restart, returned with a different boot ID, and recovered its system, service, script, lock, and data state; fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The simultaneous-invocation and interruption tests used temporary copies of the installed script and representative data. The actual production directory was nevertheless directly tested for normal/idempotent processing, busy-owner behavior without ledger mutation, restart persistence, and final recovery."]}
